  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 203 PM EDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nAnother hot July, err I mean September day on tap today, with \npoor Chattanooga notching yet another 90F day, meaning the record \nstreak of consecutive 90F days for the city continues. Relief from\nthe heatwave doesn't appear likely until next week. A very \nanomalous ridge will remain parked over the Mid-South for the next\ncouple of days, bringing significant late season heat to the \nTennessee Valley. While technically we're forecast to remain below\nheat advisory criteria, heat of this level can still bring \ndangerous effects to those who are either already vulnerable \n(whether age or medical reasons) or those who have extended times \noutdoors. Drink plenty of water!\n\nUpper ridge is forecast to retrograde into the lower Mississippi\nValley into the weekend as a weakening upper low pushes towards\nFlorida. Both features will eventually wash out as next week\nbegins. With the dissipation of the more significant ridging, we\nwill induce a slight cooling trend towards more manageable heat \nfor next week. The retrograde of the high will also likely allow \nfor the daily diurnal summer storm pulse to become reinvigorated \nas suppression weakens. As such, look for isolated to widely\nscattered rain and storm chances to return in the PM hours as we \nhead into the weekend and especially next week.",
